Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:08:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Games: Fix the player's standing on RetroAchievements
 leaderboards

Asked for a leaderboard with the player named, RetroAchievements starts
at the player's own entry on a board they have entered, and at the top
otherwise. It never sends the player's entry apart from the rows, which
is what Kodi read the standing from.

So on every board the player had entered, the leaderboards window showed
the player as the leader and "Not ranked", and the standings showed the
rows around the player instead of the top of the board.

The top of a board is now asked for without the player, and the player's
own entry with them. Estuary puts "#1" before the leader's name, so it
reads as the top of the board rather than an unexplained name.

Standings kept on disk now carry a version, so pages saved by earlier
builds, which hold the rows around the player, are fetched again.
